{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^def |FORMAT|json_bytes|evidence|question_class'\"' src/hivemind/release.py; nl -ba web/design-system/tokens.css | head -50; ls poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/old-{1,3}\"","aggregated_output":"4:A number question carries its question, its evidence in force and the marker \"Forecast unavailable\". An event or Yes/No question\n5:carries its question, its evidence and its answer labels. Nothing else is read into the package: no rung condition or bound, no\n24:FORMAT = 'hivemind-release/1'\n33:    'number': frozenset({'id', 'question', 'open', 'class', 'forecast', 'evidence'}),\n34:    'answered': frozenset({'id', 'question', 'open', 'class', 'answers', 'answer', 'evidence'}),\n35:    'evidence': frozenset({'id', 'one_line', 'quote', 'tier', 'speaker', 'original_who', 'original_day', 'sources'}),\n52:def canonical_day(text):\n64:def resolve(views_db, as_of=None):\n77:def _has_table(conn, name):\n81:def key_measure(conn, view_id, as_of):\n90:def ladder(conn, view_id):\n95:def question_class(conn, view_id, labels, as_of):\n106:def _answer(conn, view_id, as_of, positions):\n118:def _item(items_db, cache, input_id, evidence_id):\n122:            raise ReleaseRefused(f'evidence {evidence_id}: source item {input_id} is not in the items database')\n127:def _visible_views(conn, as_of):\n131:def release_export(views_db, items_db, as_of=None):\n141:            kind = question_class(views_db, view_id, labels, bound)\n148:            evidence = []\n149:            for piece in service.evidence(views_db, view_id, bound):\n152:                    item = _item(items_db, items, source['input_id'], piece['evidence_id'])\n154:                evidence.append({'id': piece['evidence_id'], **{name: piece[name] for name in EVIDENCE_TEXT}, 'sources': sources})\n155:            record['evidence'] = evidence\n157:        data = {'format': FORMAT, 'allow_list': ALLOW_LIST, 'as_of': bound, 'questions': questions}\n164:def _keys(value, kind, where):\n172:def _texts(value, names, where):\n178:def check_export(data):\n182:    if data['format'] != FORMAT or data['allow_list'] != ALLOW_LIST:\n187:    counts = {'questions': {kind: 0 for kind in CLASSES}, 'evidence': 0, 'sources': 0}\n207:        if not isinstance(question['evidence'], list):\n208:            raise ReleaseRefused(f'{where}: evidence is not a list')\n209:        for piece in question['evidence']:\n210:            _keys(piece, 'evidence', f'{where} evidence')\n211:            _texts(piece, ('id',), f'{where} evidence')\n212:            _texts(piece, EVIDENCE_TEXT, f'{where} evidence {piece[\"id\"]}')\n214:                raise ReleaseRefused(f'{where} evidence {piece[\"id\"]}: sources is not a list')\n216:                _keys(source, 'source', f'{where} evidence {piece[\"id\"]} source')\n217:                _texts(source, SOURCE_TEXT, f'{where} evidence {piece[\"id\"]} source')\n219:        counts['evidence'] += len(question['evidence'])\n226:def _open_at(conn, view_id, as_of):\n233:def _expected_evidence(views_db, items_db, view_id, as_of):\n234:    \"\"\"The evidence in force at the day, by its own SQL: visible links in link order, minus those whose latest replacement is\n237:    for link in views_db.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=? order by id', (view_id,)).fetchall():\n240:        latest = views_db.execute('select seq from replacements where old_evidence_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (link['evidence_id'],)).fetchone()\n243:        row = views_db.execute(f'select evidence_id, {\", \".join(EVIDENCE_TEXT)} from evidence where evidence_id=?', (link['evidence_id'],)).fetchone()\n245:            raise ReleaseRefused(f'{view_id}: link to evidence {link[\"evidence_id\"]}, which the store does not hold')\n247:        for source in views_db.execute('select input_id, publication_day, seq from evidence_sources where evidence_id=? order by id', (link['evidence_id'],)).fetchall():\n252:                raise ReleaseRefused(f'evidence {row[\"evidence_id\"]}: source item {source[\"input_id\"]} is not in the items database')\n254:        out.append({'id': row['evidence_id'], **{name: row[name] for name in EVIDENCE_TEXT}, 'sources': sources})\n258:def _leaves(value):\n266:def _compare(expected, actual, where):\n281:def check_origins(views_db, items_db, data, expected_as_of):\n283:    package: the day, each question's class, the questions, evidence and sources in order with their counts. Its reads are its own\n284:    SQL, apart from the identity rule (`question_class`) and the day of a sequence number (`service.visible`). Returns the number of\n296:        compared = _compare(FORMAT, data['format'], 'package.format') + _compare(ALLOW_LIST, data['allow_list'], 'package.allow_list') + 1\n301:            kind = question_class(views_db, view_id, labels, as_of)\n311:            expected_evidence = _expected_evidence(views_db, items_db, view_id, as_of)\n312:            if not isinstance(question.get('evidence'), list) or len(question['evidence']) != len(expected_evidence):\n313:                found = len(question['evidence']) if isinstance(question.get('evidence'), list) else 'no'\n314:                raise ReleaseRefused(f'question {view_id}.evidence: {found} entries where the store has {len(expected_evidence)}')\n315:            record['evidence'] = question['evidence']           # compared piece by piece below, named by the stored evidence id\n316:            compared += _compare(record, question, f'question {view_id}') - _leaves(question['evidence'])\n317:            for expected, actual in zip(expected_evidence, question['evidence']):\n318:                compared += _compare(expected, actual, f'question {view_id}.evidence {expected[\"id\"]}')\n324:def _dump(value):\n328:def stage(out_dir):\n334:def write_package(data, staged):\n342:def _no_replace_rename():\n355:def publish(staged, out_dir):\n367:def publish_report(report, path):\n386:def _unique_members(pairs):\n393:def read_data(package):\n402:def store_path(path):\n413:def _read_regular(folder, name, where):\n435:def _parse(raw, name):\n442:def check_package(path, views_db=None, items_db=None, expected_as_of=None):\n477:def withheld_unresolved(views_db, data):\n     1\t/* Shared Hivemind theme tokens. */\n     2\t:root {\n     3\t  --paper: #f5f2eb;\n     4\t  --wash: #ebe9e2;\n     5\t  --wash-strong: #e3e0d9;\n     6\t  --rule: #dfddd6;\n     7\t  --rule-strong: #c9c7c0;\n     8\t  --ink: #0f140d;\n     9\t  --ink-2: #393d36;\n    10\t  --ink-3: #6a6c65;\n    11\t  --ink-4: #9f9f98;\n    12\t  --scrim: rgba(245, 242, 235, 0.72);\n    13\t  --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(15, 20, 13, 0.04), 0 12px 32px rgba(15, 20, 13, 0.10);\n    14\t\n    15\t  --sans: \"Geist\", \"Helvetica Neue\", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\n    16\t  --mono: \"Geist Mono\", \"SF Mono\", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;\n    17\t\n    18\t  --gutter: 40px;\n    19\t  --control-height: 30px;\n    20\t  --ease: cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1);\n    21\t  color-scheme: light;\n    22\t}\npoc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/old-1:\nclosing\nforged-manifest\nforged-summary\npackage\npackage-2026-08-28\npackage-2026-08-28.report.json\npackage.report.json\n\npoc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/old-3:\npackage\npackage-2026-08-25\npackage-2026-08-25.report.json\npackage.report.json\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'D75[6-9]\\\\b' docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -24; ls docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers | tail -95\"","aggregated_output":"11823:## D756 · 2026-11-23 · Alex closes the v13s line; the first release shows number questions as \"Forecast unavailable\"\n11842:## D757 · 2026-11-23 · Toward production: the \"Forecast unavailable\" release design is ready for when Alex opens release work (council 72–72d); two choices go to Alex\n11845:  unavailable\" (D756). D726 says it \"is built with the release work, which is not started\". Council 72 agreed that opening release\n11867:## D758 · 2026-11-23 · Under D439 the council opens local release work for \"Forecast unavailable\"; non-number questions show no explanation text (§4 a); the v13s checker defects are closed as won't-fix (council 73)\n11870:  Production 方向去走了\"). He had already chosen the behaviour (D726 \"同意\"; D756 \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\"). D757 left two\n11880:     code, the line is closed (D756), and the STOP bars tuning on the 36 answers. The findings stay on record.\n11881:  4. **Order:** the exporter and the checked package first; the reader's screen second (it completes D756's screen check). How the\n11885:## D759 · 2026-11-23 · Slice 1 of the \"Forecast unavailable\" release is built and accepted at $0 (councils 74–74j design, 75–75g build); nothing committed or published\n11887:- **Under D439 and D758.** Release work was opened by council 73 (D758). This slice carries it out locally at $0. Nothing is\n11895:    Yes/No question carries its question, evidence and answer labels (D758 §4 a);\n11926:  - slice 2, the release page that reads only the package, with a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen (D756's screen check);\nround46e-brief.md\nround46f-brief.md\nround46g-brief.md\nround46h-brief.md\nround46i-brief.md\nround46j-brief.md\nround46k-brief.md\nround46l-brief.md\nround46m-brief.md\nround46