d47f-brief.md\nround47g-brief.md\nround47h-brief.md\nround48-brief.md\nround49-brief.md\nround50-brief.md\nround51-brief.md\nround52-brief.md\nround53-brief.md\nround54-brief.md\nround55-brief.md\nround56-brief.md\nround56b-brief.md\nround56c-brief.md\nround57-brief.md\nround58-brief.md\nround59-brief.md\nround60-brief.md\nround61-brief.md\nround61b-brief.md\nround62-brief.md\nround63-brief.md\nround64-brief.md\nround65-brief.md\nround66-brief.md\nround67-brief.md\nround68-brief.md\nround69-brief.md\nround69b-brief.md\nround70-brief.md\nround70b-brief.md\nround70c-brief.md\nround71-brief.md\nround72-brief.md\nround72b-brief.md\nround72c-brief.md\nround72d-brief.md\nround73-brief.md\nround74-brief.md\nround74b-brief.md\nround74c-brief.md\nround74d-brief.md\nround74e-brief.md\nround74f-brief.md\nround74g-brief.md\nround74h-brief.md\nround74i-brief.md\nround74j-brief.md\nround75-brief.md\nround75b-brief.md\nround75c-brief.md\nround75d-brief.md\nround75e-brief.md\nround75f-brief.md\nround75g-brief.md\nround76-brief.md\nround76b-brief.md\nround76c-brief.md\n83:**Split extraction sealed as a failed experiment (D378, 2026-11-06):** the split (a new-question call, an evidence call and record preparation) was benchmarked against the frozen poc-v108 and failed. Its stop line fired: helpful matters 156, 156, 159 against 166, 170, 162, with about 15% higher cost. One screened revision kept more noise than production. It is sealed in the worktree `hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review` (tag `split-extraction-failed-sealed-2026-11-06`), and nothing of it is in main. What it taught is written as proposed production experiments in `docs/prd/11-production-experiments-from-split.md`: E1 no-home helpful drops, E2 duplicate questions, E3 ladder checks with D186, E4 judge refusals, E5 D203's revision day, E6 the measurement kit. Each opens only on Alex's word.\n448:**The one next task: slice 2 of the \"Forecast unavailable\" release, the reader's screen (D758 order; D756's screen check).** The release\n450:submission. A browser check shows the `old-1/v8` screen with its question, its sources and \"Forecast unavailable\", and nothing else. It\n453:**Slice 1 is built and accepted at $0 (D759).**\n473:**Earlier next task (done, D759): build slice 1 once its design passes council 74 (D758).**\n482:**Earlier next task (done, D757): when release work opens, a $0 check of the reader's screen for number questions (D756).** On a\n494:unavailable\". When release work opens, the first step is a $0 check of the reader's screen.\n856:    - removing the previous conclusion misses its screen by one, and the frozen gold reads 44.3 against 45.0;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import json,pathlib,collections; base=pathlib.Path(\\\"poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g\\\"); pairs=[(\\\"old-1/package\\\",\\\"v8\\\"),(\\\"old-3/package-2026-08-25\\\",\\\"v36\\\"),(\\\"old-1/package-2026-08-28\\\",\\\"v10\\\")];\nfor folder,key in pairs:\n raw=(base/folder/\\\"release-data.json\\\").read_bytes(); data=json.loads(raw); q=next(q for q in data[\\\"questions\\\"] if q[\\\"id\\\"]==key); evidence=q[\\\"evidence\\\"]; print(folder,data[\\\"as_of\\\"],len(data[\\\"questions\\\"]),{k:v for k,v in q.items() if k\"'!=\"evidence\"},len(evidence)); print(\"first\",evidence[0]); print(\"source count\",collections.Counter(len(e[\"sources\"]) for e in evidence)); print(\"empty source values\", collections.Counter(k for e in evidence for s in e[\"sources\"] for k,v in s.items() if not v)); print(\"escape overhead\", sum((6-len(x.encode()))*raw.count(x.encode()) for x in \"<>&'\"\\\\u2028\\\\u2029\\\"))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import json,pathlib,collections; base=pathlib.Path(\\\"poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g\\\"); pairs=[(\\\"old-1/package\\\",\\\"v8\\\"),(\\\"old-3/package-2026-08-25\\\",\\\"v36\\\"),(\\\"old-1/package-2026-08-28\\\",\\\"v10\\\")];\nfor folder,key in pairs:\n raw=(base/folder/\\\"release-data.json\\\").read_bytes(); data=json.loads(raw); q=next(q for q in data[\\\"questions\\\"] if q[\\\"id\\\"]==key); evidence=q[\\\"evidence\\\"]; print(folder,data[\\\"as_of\\\"],len(data[\\\"questions\\\"]),{k:v for k,v in q.items() if k\"'!=\"evidence\"},len(evidence)); print(\"first\",evidence[0]); print(\"source count\",collections.Counter(len(e[\"sources\"]) for e in evidence)); print(\"empty source values\", collections.Counter(k for e in evidence for s in e[\"sources\"] for k,v in s.items() if not v)); print(\"escape overhead\", sum((6-len(x.encode()))*raw.count(x.encode()) for x in \"<>&'\"\\\\u2028\\\\u2029\\\"))'\"","aggregated_output":"old-1/package 2026-09-20 47 {'id': 'v8', 'question': 'How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?', 'open': True, 'class': 'number', 'forecast': 'Forecast unavailable'} 1284\nfirst {'id': 'e109', 'one_line': 'NVIDIA’s Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenue in fiscal Q1 2027, equal to 92% of total sales.', 'quote': 'During the first quarter of fiscal 2027, the Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenues, accounting for 92% of total sales.', 'tier': 'fact', 'speaker': 'tradingview.com', 'original_who': 'NVIDIA', 'original_day': '', 'sources': [{'title': 'NVIDIA Falls 7% in a Month: Should You Still Hold NVDA Stock or Exit?', 'publisher': 'tradingview.com', 'day': '2026-07-06', 'uri': 'https://www.tradingview.com/news/zacks:85d73237b094b:0-nvidia-falls-7-in-a-month-should-you-still-hold-nvda-stock-or-exit/'}]}\nsource count Counter({1: 1284})\nempty source values Counter()\nescape overhead 955\nold-3/package-2026-08-25 2026-08-25 36 {'id': 'v36', 'question': 'Will NVIDIA begin shipping Rubin Ultra by December 31, 2027?', 'open': True, 'class': 'event', 'answers': ['Yes', 'No'], 'answer': 'Yes'} 1\nfirst {'id': 'e2419', 'one_line': 'The Information reported that NVIDIA is testing at least three Rubin Ultra versions with 192GB to 256GB of high-bandwidth memory, versus the originally announced 1 terabyte.', 'quote': 'According to The Information, the company has been testing at least three versions with reduced high-bandwidth memory, some as low as 192GB to 256GB, well below the 1 terabyte Jensen Huang originally announced.', 'tier': 'rumour', 'speaker': 'Insider Monkey', 'original_who': 'The Information', 'original_day': '', 'sources': [{'title': 'NVIDIA Corporation (NVDA) & Advanced Micro Devices (AMD): Nvidia Might Ship AI Chips With Less Memory. AMD Says It’s Not Worried', 'publisher': 'insidermonkey.com', 'day': '2026-08-21', 'uri': 'https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/nvidia-corporation-nvda-advanced-micro-204025825.html'}]}\nsource count Counter({1: 1})\nempty source values Counter()\nescape overhead 685\nold-1/package-2026-08-28 2026-08-28 35 {'id': 'v10', 'question': 'Will NVIDIA complete an investment in Firmus Technologies’ preference shares by December 31, 2026?', 'open': True, 'class': 'event', 'answers': ['Yes', 'No'], 'answer': 'Yes'} 1\nfirst {'id': 'e217', 'one_line': 'NVIDIA has indicated interest in about US$500 million of Firmus preference shares, intended to convert to ordinary equity at Firmus’ IPO later in 2026.', 'quote': 'Street Talk can reveal that the $US4.9 trillion chip developer has put up its hand for about $US500 million ($721 million) worth of Firmus’ preference shares, which are designed to convert to ordinary equity at the initial public offering later this year.', 'tier': 'rumour', 'speaker': 'afr.com, citing Street Talk', 'original_who': 'afr.com / Street Talk (unnamed sources)', 'original_day': '', 'sources': [{'title': 'Nvidia tips $720m into Firmus’ $2.9b raising; share split under way', 'publisher': 'afr.com', 'day': '2026-07-08', 'uri': 'https://www.afr.com/street-talk/nvidia-tips-us500m-into-firmus-s-us2b-raising-share-split-underway-20260709-p60dv9'}]}\nsource count Counter({1: 1})\nempty source values Counter()\nescape overhead 660\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
