{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '11823,11903p'; nl -ba docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | sed -n '448,454p'\"","aggregated_output":" 11823\t## D756 · 2026-11-23 · Alex closes the v13s line; the first release shows number questions as \"Forecast unavailable\"\n 11824\t\n 11825\t- **The question** (after D755): \"付费重发的结论是“停”：luna 在新格式下格式错误多（36 个首发里 22 个被拒），在说不清的题上还会硬给数；不过“两题合在一起算”确实避免了自相矛盾。数字题这条线下一步怎么走？\"\n 11826\t  - Options:\n 11827\t    - \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线 (推荐)\": the council's consensus;\n 11828\t    - \"换更强的模型再小测一次\": a stronger model or higher effort, with a small paid probe and a cap Alex names;\n 11829\t    - \"先停，我想谈谈\".\n 11830\t- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-23): \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线 (推荐)\".\n 11831\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n 11832\t  - The v13s judge line ends at its STOP. Nothing from it enters the product, and poc-v118 stays the product (D690).\n 11833\t  - The first release carries D726: number questions show the question and its sources with \"Forecast unavailable\", the band, the\n 11834\t    forecast text and the history withheld together.\n 11835\t  - The one next step, when release work opens, is a $0 check of the reader's screen on a stored number question that has a\n 11836\t    forecast and history: only the question, its sources and \"Forecast unavailable\" appear.\n 11837\t- **Kept for the record, not built:**\n 11838\t  - the D725 consistency finding (separate answers contradicted each other in 8 of 9 pairs, joint answers in none);\n 11839\t  - the open checker defects in `PAID-V13S-RESULT.md` §5;\n 11840\t  - the v13s request and harness in `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/`.\n 11841\t\n 11842\t## D757 · 2026-11-23 · Toward production: the \"Forecast unavailable\" release design is ready for when Alex opens release work (council 72–72d); two choices go to Alex\n 11843\t\n 11844\t- **Why.** Alex's direction tonight was to converge and head toward production (D750), and he chose to release with \"Forecast\n 11845\t  unavailable\" (D756). D726 says it \"is built with the release work, which is not started\". Council 72 agreed that opening release\n 11846\t  work is Alex's call, so tonight's step is the design, not the build.\n 11847\t- **The gap, measured at $0** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` §1):\n 11848\t  - today every reader of a number question can see its forecast: the service, the idea input, the closing text;\n 11849\t  - Yes/No and event explanations can quote number forecasts (`old-3/v36` judgement 799, `old-1/v10` judgement 865).\n 11850\t- **The design, after four review rounds** (`codex-r72.md` … `codex-r72d.md`):\n 11851\t  - one release exporter with an explicit allow-list, called directly by the release builder; the finished package is checked;\n 11852\t  - for a number question, the allow-list holds only the question, its sources and \"Forecast unavailable\";\n 11853\t  - the release reads nothing else: no live POC service, no translated or prepared JSON, no composite trials;\n 11854\t  - identity is structural: a question is a number question unless it is an event measure or a canonical Yes/No pair, and unresolved\n 11855\t    records are withheld and listed. Verified on four stores with no wrong result;\n 11856\t  - tests, mutants and an end-to-end acceptance on `old-1/v8` and the two known event leaks.\n 11857\t  - **Why an allow-list.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new leak paths in a reader-by-reader design, so revision 3 replaced that\n 11858\t    approach with one structural rule.\n 11859\t- **Open for Alex:**\n 11860\t  1. whether to open release work now (then: build to this design, then the $0 release check);\n 11861\t  2. what questions that are not number questions show in the release:\n 11862\t     - (a) answer and label without explanation text, recommended by the council and Claude;\n 11863\t     - (b) explanations only where the judge was shown no number question's state: 21 of 85 questions at the latest answer, and it\n 11864\t       cannot guarantee that no number forecast is quoted.\n 11865\t- **Not done.** Nothing is built and nothing is committed. The POC is unchanged.\n 11866\t\n 11867\t## D758 · 2026-11-23 · Under D439 the council opens local release work for \"Forecast unavailable\"; non-number questions show no explanation text (§4 a); the v13s checker defects are closed as won't-fix (council 73)\n 11868\t\n 11869\t- **Why the council decides.** Alex is asleep and delegated tonight's decisions (D750: \"这边的决策交给你，还有 Council … 准备要往\n 11870\t  Production 方向去走了\"). He had already chosen the behaviour (D726 \"同意\"; D756 \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\"). D757 left two\n 11871\t  choices for him; under D439 a choice that would go to Alex goes to the council when it is reversible and within the limits.\n 11872\t- **Council round 73** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round73-brief.md`, `codex-r73.md`, `claude-r73.md`), consensus:\n 11873\t  1. **Release work opens tonight, local and at $0:** the exporter, the release builder, the package check, tests and mutants, the $0\n 11874\t     release check. Nothing committed, pushed, published or deployed; the POC and colleagues' page unchanged. Reversible: the package\n 11875\t     can be deleted without touching what the POC serves. D726's \"not started\" described the state on 2026-11-22 and set no gate.\n 11876\t  2. **§4 (a):** an event or Yes/No question shows its question, evidence and answer with its original label, and no generated\n 11877\t     explanation. It alone guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose (option (b) cannot: a request carries the\n 11878\t     question's earlier reasoning, `views/judging.py:211`). The cost is real: readers lose the written rationale for those answers.\n 11879\t  3. **The v13s checker defects** (`PAID-V13S-RESULT.md` §5) are closed as won't-fix: `calc_small.py` has callers only in research\n 11880\t     code, the line is closed (D756), and the STOP bars tuning on the 36 answers. The findings stay on record.\n 11881\t  4. **Order:** the exporter and the checked package first; the reader's screen second (it completes D756's screen check). How the\n 11882\t     idea path enters the release is settled in the build design's review (round 74).\n 11883\t- **Still Alex's:** commit, push, publish, deploy, colleagues' POC page, any paid send or judge work.\n 11884\t\n 11885\t## D759 · 2026-11-23 · Slice 1 of the \"Forecast unavailable\" release is built and accepted at $0 (councils 74–74j design, 75–75g build); nothing committed or published\n 11886\t\n 11887\t- **Under D439 and D758.** Release work was opened by council 73 (D758). This slice carries it out locally at $0. Nothing is\n 11888\t  committed, pushed, published or deployed. The POC is unchanged: no POC code imports the release module.\n 11889\t- **The design** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md`):\n 11890\t  - revision 10 was ready per council 74j, after ten rounds (74 to 74j);\n 11891\t  - revision 11 records the build changes required by councils 75 to 75f.\n 11892\t\n 11893\t  It holds:\n 11894\t  - one allow-listed exporter: a number question carries its question, its evidence in force and \"Forecast unavailable\"; an event or\n 11895\t    Yes/No question carries its question, evidence and answer labels (D758 §4 a);\n 11896\t  - the writer refuses an off-list field;\n 11897\t  - the pass condition: every package field compared with its stored source at the bound, derived from the store;\n 11898\t  - a staged check before one atomic no-replace publication (`renamex_np` with `RENAME_EXCL`);\n 11899\t  - reports published by a no-replace link;\n 11900\t  - canonical days; keys counted only once visible at the bound; store paths free of URI syntax; package files read once.\n 11901\t- **Built:** `src/hivemind/release.py`, `scripts/release_build.py`, `tests/test_release.py`.\n 11902\t- **Proof** (`RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md`):\n 11903\t  - 36 release tests;\n   448\t**The one next task: slice 2 of the \"Forecast unavailable\" release, the reader's screen (D758 order; D756's screen check).** The release\n   449\tpage reads only the slice-1 package: no live service, no `/library` fetch, no translated JSON, no composite trials, and no idea\n   450\tsubmission. A browser check shows the `old-1/v8` screen with its question, its sources and \"Forecast unavailable\", and nothing else. It\n   451\tstarts with a design reviewed by the council before code, like slice 1. Commit, publish and deploy remain Alex's.\n   452\t\n   453\t**Slice 1 is built and accepted at $0 (D759).**\n   454\t- Code: `src/hivemind/release.py`, `scripts/release_build.py`, `tests/test_release.py`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r76.md | head -90; rg -n 'presentation rules|Presentation rules|metadata separator' docs/poc/thesis-ui.md; rg -n '(visibility|opacity|:before|::before|::after)' web --glob '*.css' | head -50\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r76.md | head -90; rg -n 'presentation rules|Presentation rules|metadata separator' docs/poc/thesis-ui.md; rg -n '(visibility|opacity|:before|::before|::after)' web --glob '*.css' | head -50\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t**Verdict: not ready to build.** The package check is sound, but the screen check could pass a page that says “1284 pieces of evidence” and shows only one summary. It could also reject a correct page because five genuine source titles contain “Bullish.” [RELEASE-PAGE.md:134](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:134) · [RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:145](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:145)\n     2\t\n     3\t1. **An ordinary source link breaks the zero-request promise.** I counted 1,258 HTTP(S) source entries under `old-1/v8`. Clicking one can navigate from the local file to the publisher. `noopener noreferrer` suppresses opener and referrer information. It still permits navigation. Opening `<details>` itself needs no request. For the promise written in §0, render the source address as plain text and check that expanding the evidence creates no navigable links. The `file://` test can then run with Chrome’s normal file restrictions. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:16](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:16) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:64](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:64) · [CSP navigation directives](https://www.w3.org/TR/CSP3/#directives-navigation)\n     4\t\n     5\t2. **The specified JSON escaping leaves the closing tag intact.** I checked the file bytes. Line 38 gives the same literal characters on both sides of “escaped as.” A source containing `</script>` can therefore end the data block before the page script reads it. Specify the literal JSON escape sequences `\\u003c`, `\\u003e`, `\\u0026`, `\\u2028` and `\\u2029`. Declare UTF-8 at the start of the file and put the CSP before the style, script and embedded data. Test the existing fixture in the browser with its evidence expanded. Its exact quote must be visible as text, with no image element created. The proposed “no second `<script>` start” check misses the closing tag, and parsing JSON alone never exercises the proposed `innerHTML` mutant. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:37](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:37) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:104](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:104) · [HTML script parsing](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#restrictions-for-contents-of-script-elements) · [CSP meta placement](https://www.w3.org/TR/CSP3/#meta-element)\n     6\t\n     7\t3. **Keep byte-for-byte rendering and format 2. Update the checks that depend on format 1.** Read all three files once through the open directory handle. Hash and compare those same page bytes against `render_page(raw_data)` using the same data bytes that passed the store check. That certifies the inspected copy. Adding a required file and manifest member justifies `/2` while the data allow-list stays `/1`. The existing acceptance script pins `/1`, and two helpers that deliberately alter data refresh only the data hash. Their format-2 copies must also regenerate the page and its hash so the forged forecast still reaches the store comparison. Add the converse case too: a correct page with only `page_sha256` wrong must fail for that exact reason. Every proposed page-tampering test refreshes that hash, so deleting the hash check currently escapes them. [release.py:454](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:454) · [release_check.py:24](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:24) · [release_check.py:128](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:128) · [test_release.py:180](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:180) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:109](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:109)\n     8\t\n     9\t4. **Check what the reader sees both before and after expanding `v8`.** Pin the exact question, “How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?”, alongside the three stated labels. For the expanded card, freeze the expected ordered evidence and source values from the accepted package before the run. Compare the displayed entries with that expectation, including the full Morningstar quote and attribution. This catches missing, duplicated or misplaced entries and permits “Bullish” exactly where the source used it. Close and reopen the card once to catch a second copy being appended. Apply the same discipline to the two dated cards: pin the day and question, require “Answer: Yes,” expand their evidence, and check the known explanation phrases there too. A collapsed page-text search cannot inspect content the script has yet to create. [FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:134](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:134) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:69](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:69) · [release_check.py:173](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:173) · [RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:60](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:60)\n    10\t\n    11\t5. **Credit the fetch test only when Chrome identifies the attempted connection.** The Chrome 158 probe recorded in the design answers the CDP question for this Mac: the blocked fetch produced two log errors and zero `Network.requestWillBeSent` events. Recompute the altered inline script’s CSP hash so the test script actually runs. Require the normal card to render and the security event to name the intended destination and `connect-src`. A stale script hash would otherwise earn credit for blocking the whole script. Port 9 also has an independent browser block, so a generic fetch error there proves too little. Enable observation before navigation and keep it active through expansion. If “zero console errors” remains a condition, include `Runtime.consoleAPICalled` for `console.error`. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:130](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:130) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:144](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:144) · [Fetch port blocking](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#port-blocking) · [CDP console events](https://chromedevtools.github.io/devtools-protocol/tot/Runtime/#event-consoleAPICalled)\n    12\t\n    13\t6. **Correct two browser acceptance conditions.** A blocked inline script leaves browser scripting enabled, so `<noscript>` stays hidden. If the reader should see a fallback in that case, put ordinary visible text in the page and replace it after successful rendering. The 3-second and size budgets **are** set before the first screen control. Start the timer at navigation and stop when the full expected list is visible. Starting at `load` can omit the work of parsing and rendering the embedded data. The state table also promises a phone-width and dark-scheme check that §6 never performs. Either define its viewport and observable pass condition or remove the acceptance claim. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:79](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:79) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:155](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:155) · [HTML `noscript` behavior](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#the-noscript-element)\n    14\t\n    15\tThe separate release page fits D758 and requires no POC change. The text filter is optional for D756. I would leave it out of this slice so acceptance covers the reader’s actual task: opening a question and seeing all its sources with the forecast withheld. This was a read-only review. The Chrome observation above comes from the probe recorded in the design. [D756:11833](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11833) · [D758:11881](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11881) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:59](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:59)7:## Presentation rules\n9:Use sentence case for interface labels, navigation, section titles and controls, except Alex's explicit tab names `Thesis Library` and `Explore Ideas` (D327). Never force interface text to all capitals. Preserve the spelling of tickers, acronyms, proper names and quoted source text. Separate adjacent metadata fields with `|`, using the shared separator; do not use middle dots or bullets as metadata separators.\nweb/design-system/design-system.css:13:*, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }\nweb/design-system/design-system.css:82:.ticker[aria-current=\"page\"]::after {\nweb/design-system/design-system.css:131:@keyframes enter { from { transform: translateX(24px); opacity: 0; } to { transform: none; opacity: 1; } }\nweb/design-system/design-system.css:132:@keyframes fade { from { opacity: 0; } to { opacity: 1; } }\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
