{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"agent_message","text":"**Not ready to build.** Revision 3 catches the extra forecast line from round 76b when it appears inside the `v8` card. Put the same line immediately above the card and the reader still sees “Forecast: $361 billion,” while every card comparison passes. D756 requires checking what appears on the reader’s screen. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:187](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:187) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:207](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:207) · [DECISIONS-log.md:11835](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11835)\n\n| Round‑76b finding | Revision‑3 assessment |\n|---|---|\n| 1. Source links | **Closed.** Addresses appear as plain text. The expanded page must contain zero links, `href` attributes, or `src` attributes. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:91](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:91) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:198](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:198) |\n| 2. Embedded JSON | **Closed.** The design specifies the literal escapes and header order. The browser must display the exact fixture quote with no image element. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:57](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:57) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:210](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:210) |\n| 3. Format 2 and package checks | **Closed.** The checker compares and hashes the same page bytes. A correct page with only its recorded hash wrong must fail. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:73](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:73) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:143](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:143) |\n| 4. What the cards show | **Partly closed.** The `v8` comparison preserves all 1,284 evidence groups and their order. The dated-package correction is closed. I verified that August 25 `old-3/v36` asks about Rubin Ultra and August 28 `old-1/v10` asks about Firmus. Each has “Yes,” one evidence entry, and one source. The screen comparison still has the gap described below. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:174](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:174) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:193](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:193) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:201](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:201) |\n| 5. Blocked fetch | **Closed.** Observation begins before navigation. The altered script must render the list, and Chrome’s security error must identify both the destination and `connect-src`. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:167](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:167) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:213](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:213) |\n| 6. Browser acceptance conditions | **Partly closed.** The fallback, phone width, and literal dark and light colours are specified. The timer can still stop while the list is invisible. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:49](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:49) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:226](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:226) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:232](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:232) |\n\n**Two corrections are needed before build.**\n\n1. **Check the complete screen, including the text around the selected card.** Freeze the expected header and collapsed question list, then compare the page again with the selected card expanded. Keep the existing evidence grouping. Require the extra-line test to fail when the line is a sibling of `v8`. The card’s text-node walk also misses words drawn by CSS `::before` or `::after`. For this fixed template, requiring all reader-facing words to come from text nodes and checking that its stylesheet generates no text closes that gap. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:84](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:84) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:187](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:187) · [W3C generated-content specification](https://www.w3.org/TR/css-pseudo-4/#generated-content)\n\n2. **Use the same visibility test for the evidence and the three-second timer.** A list with `opacity: 0` still has non-zero boxes. Its text passes the stated card-reading conditions, and removing the fallback satisfies the timer’s other condition. Check visibility through ancestors, including zero opacity, and require every expected question before stopping the timer. A copy with the list fully transparent should miss the deadline even though all its cards exist. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:187](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:187) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:232](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:232) · [CSSOM visibility algorithm](https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom-view/#dom-element-checkvisibility)\n\nI found no additional request path or implementation blocker in the specified page. This was a read-only design review. Slice 2 has no implementation yet, so its browser behavior remains unverified. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:3)"}}
